hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"41","Subḥāna Rabbiya ‘l-a`lā. Glory is to my Lord, the Most High. (This is said three times in Arabic.) Reference: Abu Dawud, Ibn Majah, An-Nasa'i, At-Tirmidhi, and Ahmad. See also Al-Albani, Sahih At-Tirmidhi 1/83."
"42","Subḥānaka Allāhumma Rabbanā wa biḥamdika Allāhumma ‘ghfir lī. Glory is to You, O Allah, our Lord, and praise is Yours. O Allah, forgive me. Reference: Al-Bukhari and Muslim, see invocation no. 34 above."
